### 6. Dynamic Department Map (LinkedHashMap Loop)

* **Question:** Write an interactive program using a `LinkedHashMap` and a `Scanner` inside a loop to keep asking the user for department names and HODs until they type `"n"` to stop.
* **Answer:**
```java
Scanner scan = new Scanner(System.in);
LinkedHashMap<String, String> map = new LinkedHashMap<>();

while(true) {
    System.out.println("Enter the department name:");
    String dName = scan.next();

    System.out.println("Enter the department HOD:");
    String dHod = scan.next();

    map.put(dName, dHod);

    System.out.println("Do you want to continue? type y-yes OR n-no");
    String optionChoosen = scan.next().toLowerCase();
    if(optionChoosen.equals("n")) {
        break;
    }
}
System.out.println(map);

```



