### 7. Interactive Reverse TreeMap Keys

* **Question:** Write an interactive program using a `TreeMap` with `Collections.reverseOrder()` to take department and HOD inputs from a user, and print only the keys (`keySet()`) sorted in reverse alphabetical order.
* **Answer:**
```java
Scanner scan = new Scanner(System.in);
TreeMap<String, String> map = new TreeMap<>(Collections.reverseOrder());

while(true) {
    System.out.println("Enter the department name:");
    String dName = scan.next();

    System.out.println("Enter the department HOD:");
    String dHod = scan.next();

    map.put(dName, dHod);

    System.out.println("Do you want to continue? type y-yes OR n-no");
    String optionChoosen = scan.next().toLowerCase();
    if(optionChoosen.equals("n")) {
        break;
    }
}
System.out.println(map.keySet());

```



