### 8. Iterating Sorted TreeMap (Default A-Z Order)

* **Question:** Create a `TreeMap` with preset Indian departments and HODs, and use `map.entrySet()` inside a loop to print them neatly in default alphabetical order.
* **Answer:**
```java
TreeMap<String, String> map = new TreeMap<>();
map.put("Physics", "Dr. H. J. Bhabha");
map.put("Mathematics", "Dr. C. S. Seshadri");
map.put("Computer Science", "Dr. A. K. Choudhury");
map.put("Chemistry", "Dr. C. N. R. Rao");

for(Map.Entry<String, String> i : map.entrySet()) {
    System.out.println("Department Name: " + i.getKey() + " Department HOD: " + i.getValue());
}

```



